                <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='9'>&apos; is selected, the coloring is based on the last Dimension in view per Date Granularity on this tab. By default the last Dimension in view is </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='9'>&apos;CR Level 2&apos;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='9'> and  Date Granularity is </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='9'>&apos;Weekly&apos;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='9'>
If you click on [-] on CR level 1, then the coloring will be based on CR level 1 and Weekly
If you click on [+] on CR level 2, then the coloring will be based on CR level 3 and Weekly</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='shape' value='Bug Tracking/light.png' />
                <format attr='size' value='2.022099494934082' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
